WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.640
Horror fans have a lot to look forward to
over the next couple of years, with a growing

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.630
slate of sequels to smash hits, original projects
from trusted filmmakers, and even a couple

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.610
of exciting remakes on the rise.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:16.880
2019 in particular looks to be a strong year
for the genre, so let's take a look at what

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.210
the kind-of-distant future will bring for
fright fans.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.210
An American Werewolf in London

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:27.740
John Landis' landmark 1981 film established
him as a daring filmmaker with a strong visual

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:32.270
style and proved that he could successfully
blend gut-wrenching horror with comedy.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:37.010
So, remaking An American Werewolf in London
might seem like a risky proposition for most

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:38.010
filmmakers.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.059
But with the original auteur's son, Max, is
ready to take on the task, and he has his

00:00:42.059 --> 00:00:43.950
father's blessing … sort of.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.129
The elder Landis told Collider:

00:00:45.129 --> 00:00:49.329
"I know it won't be as bad as An American
Werewolf In Paris, which was sh-t."

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:51.969
"Oh, be serious, would you?!"

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:53.180
Firestarter

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:57.629
Stephen King's Firestarter, a story about
a young girl with powerful pyrokinetic abilities

00:00:57.629 --> 00:01:02.770
on the run from sinister government agents,
was adapted in 1984 with a young Drew Barrymore

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:03.770
in the lead.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:08.090
While it's one the more faithful adaptations
of King's work, it hasn't aged perfectly,

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:11.820
so Blumhouse Productions is ready to give
the story a fresh new look.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:16.240
One potential hiccup is that screenwriter
Akiva Goldsman is attached to direct.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.140
Goldsman had a pretty major setback in 2017
when his screenplay for King's Dark Tower

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:25.850
failed to resonate with fans, but maybe he'll
turn things around with the new Firestarter.

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.230
It: Chapter Two

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:31.470
An even stronger Stephen King story in the
pipeline is the sequel to It.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:35.869
The first chapter blew everyone away at the
box office, but Warner Bros. didn't greenlight

00:01:35.869 --> 00:01:39.670
the second installment until they were absolutely
sure the film would be a hit.

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:43.299
Which means even though fans are clamoring
for a follow-up, there's still a lot of work

00:01:43.299 --> 00:01:44.430
to be done.

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:48.900
Director Andy Muschietti is all but guaranteed
to return and says that the film will center

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:53.431
around the adult lives of the Losers as they
return to Derry to battle Pennywise... but

00:01:53.431 --> 00:01:57.020
that we can expect to see all of those cute
kiddos from the first film, too.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:02.100
It: Chapter Two is scheduled to hit theaters
on September 6th, 2019.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.200
The Crooked Man

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:08.890
In addition to a new installment of The Conjuring,
2019 will also deliver another spin-off-slash-sequel

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:09.920
in The Crooked Man.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.250
Based on one of the creepiest scenes from
The Conjuring 2, the film is expected to flesh

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.180
out the Crooked Man's backstory.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:20.849
Between this, The Nun, and the continued chills
brought on by the Annabelle series, the Conjuring

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:25.510
universe is expanding into even scarier new
territory with every take.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.420
Untitled Wizard of Oz movie

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:31.930
The Wicked Witch of the West is pretty frightening,
and goodness knows the world of L. Frank Baum

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.800
got wild in Return to Oz.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:38.160
But now New Line Cinema is ready to see Oz
get even darker with a Wizard of Oz-centric

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.160
horror film.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:42.780
The film will be written by newcomer Mike
Van Waes who's already showed some promise

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:45.720
in Hollywood with a black list script called
Hammerspace.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:50.160
With all the anthropomorphic creatures and
conniving wizards already lurking around Oz,

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.220
it's not too hard to imagine the world getting
very, very grim.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:57.660
"I even scare myself!"

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.129
Untitled Joss Whedon WWII film

00:03:00.129 --> 00:03:03.640
Joss Whedon has been tied up in the realm
of superheroes lately, but he's still got

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.739
the gift of making edgy horror fare.

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:10.590
In 2019, he's returning to the fright fold
at last with a new historical horror film.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.590
He told Complex:

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:14.020
"It's as dark as anything I've ever written.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:18.460
It's a historical fiction-slash-horror movie
about a time when the world was going insane."

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:23.520
Whedon went on to discuss the "eerie" parallels
he uncovered between 1930s Germany and the

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:28.810
modern-day United States, so count on this
one to be creepy and a little too timely for

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:29.810
comfort.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:30.810
The Blob

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:35.790
The 1958 low-budget horror classic The Blob
has already gotten the remake treatment once,

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:36.790
in 1988.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:41.470
That version was pretty inessential, but with
Samuel L. Jackson and Halle Berry reportedly

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:44.920
starring in a new take, things are about to
get even quirkier.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:49.069
Action director Simon West has long been attached
to the project, but we'll have to wait to

00:03:49.069 --> 00:03:50.849
see how The Blob takes shape.

00:03:50.849 --> 00:03:55.430
But with Jackson on board to star, we can
probably count on some wonderfully weird one-liners.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:04:01.409
"I have had it with these motherf----ing snakes
on this motherf---ing plane."

00:04:01.409 --> 00:04:02.409
Glass

00:04:02.409 --> 00:04:04.659
If you haven't seen Split yet, spoiler alert.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:06.040
You may want to skip ahead.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:07.220
Still there?

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:09.460
"Oh, okay."

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.390
Split was certainly anchored by James McAvoy's
mesmerizing performance, but it's the film's

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:16.599
last act that really sticks the landing.

00:04:16.599 --> 00:04:20.910
In the final scene, Bruce Willis makes an
unexpected return as David Dunn, the hero

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:25.390
of 2000's Unbreakable, and ties the world
of the Beast into the world of Samuel L. Jackson's

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:26.390
Mr. Glass.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:28.740
M. Night Shyamalan has never been a sequel
guy.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:33.370
So, it was a shock to see that those two films
are not only connected, but that a third installment

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.220
of the Unbreakable series called Glass is
on the way, too.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:41.910
The cast will feature Willis, Jackson, McAvoy
and Anya Taylor-Joy all reprising their roles,

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:46.259
and it will be the final installment of the
dark superhero trilogy that has suddenly taken

00:04:46.259 --> 00:04:47.259
shape.

00:04:47.259 --> 00:04:50.770
Glass will hit theaters on January 18, 2019.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:51.770
Eli

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:56.400
Writer David Chirchirillo contributed one
of the most brutally satisfying segments of

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:00.400
the 2014 horror anthology ABC's of Death 2.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:05.360
And his screenplay for Eli garnered some attention
after making the 2015 Black List.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:10.241
The film centers on a sick boy who experiences
ghostly goings-on at a secluded clinic, and

00:05:10.241 --> 00:05:15.150
with Sinister 2's Ciaran Foy at the helm,
Eli could be a sleeper hit in the making.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:16.150
Hellboy

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:21.240
Fans had long held out hope for a third installment
of director Guillermo Del Toro's Hellboy series,

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:25.731
but that hope was unfortunately dashed when
Del Toro finally admitted early in 2017 that

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:27.440
it just wasn't going to happen.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.680
"Sorry, lady!"

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:34.080
But that doesn't mean moviegoers have seen
the last of the Right Hand of Doom.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:39.010
Director Neil Marshall, best known for his
nerve-jangling 2005 thriller The Descent,

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:41.270
will be taking the helm of the R-rated reboot.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:45.290
And Stranger Things' David Harbour has already
impressed with a first-glimpse of his physique

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:46.720
for the title role.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:51.040
Count on having a hell of a good time when
Hellboy hits theaters on January 11th.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:52.910
Untitled Jordan Peele project

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:57.090
Last but not least, Jordan Peele is returning
to the horror scene in 2019.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:01.910
His directorial debut Get Out was one of the
most talked-about movies of 2017, so there's

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:05.290
a lot of excitement already building around
what he may do next.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:09.410
Peele is expected to deliver another socially
charged horror film, and told ScreenJunkies:

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:14.030
"The worst monster that you can explore in
a horror movie is human beings themselves."

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:17.400
"I think the scariest thing we don't talk
about enough is that when people get together,

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:19.740
we're… capable of the darkest things."

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:23.289
Peele's new pic will drop on March 15th, 2019.

00:06:23.289 --> 00:06:24.500
Thanks for watching!

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.220
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.460
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

